WEBVTT

00:06.631 --> 00:10.218
[sweet airy music]

00:42.876 --> 00:46.004
[Ung] "His drawings
that exhibit his emotions

00:46.087 --> 00:48.214
are similar to the doodles

00:48.298 --> 00:50.592
of a child trapped in his own world."

00:52.927 --> 00:55.263
And there you have it, folks, 

00:55.346 --> 00:57.557
my entire life summed up in one sentence.

00:57.640 --> 00:58.683
I took pity on you.

01:00.727 --> 01:03.438
It seemed like
your life was so meaningless

01:04.689 --> 01:06.566
that you abandoned things so easily.

01:07.067 --> 01:10.361
What would your life be
if you kept living it like that?

01:11.196 --> 01:14.240
[Ung] Honestly,
what he said hit home hard.

01:14.324 --> 01:17.702
WITH UNG

01:19.287 --> 01:20.580
THE UNBEARABLE LIGHTNESS OF BEING

01:20.663 --> 01:23.750
Hmm, I wanna live an easy life.
You know, just peaceful and carefree.

01:23.833 --> 01:25.085
[chuckles]

01:25.877 --> 01:26.878
[Yeon-su] Excuse me, ma'am?

01:26.961 --> 01:28.630
[Yeon-su] What's your school ranking?

01:28.713 --> 01:29.839
[Ung] I'm 267th.

01:29.923 --> 01:31.466
How many students are here?

01:31.549 --> 01:33.760
267 students.

01:34.844 --> 01:35.804
[breathes in sharply]

01:35.887 --> 01:37.180
Drawing is just like a hobby to me.

01:37.764 --> 01:38.681
What I want,

01:38.765 --> 01:42.519
is to bask in the sun during the day
and to lay underneath a lamp at nighttime.

01:42.602 --> 01:44.521
A life of stress just isn't for me.

01:47.565 --> 01:48.858
- [teacher] What's wrong with you?
- I can draw a new one.

01:48.942 --> 01:50.902
[professor] Choi Ung,
don't you have any ambition?

01:52.195 --> 01:55.532
[Ung] Someone needs this chance
more than I do. Give it to them.

01:55.615 --> 01:57.951
[Ji-ung] Don't pull back.
I want your innermost thoughts

01:58.034 --> 02:00.578
about your work, your process,
about your life as an artist,

02:00.662 --> 02:02.705
you can talk about
your future plans and goals.

02:04.707 --> 02:05.875
I don't really have any.

02:07.210 --> 02:09.838
[Ung] That's how I lived.
Always been that way.

02:12.549 --> 02:16.427
Hey Ung, you're very lucky. You're so
young, but you already have a restaurant.

02:16.511 --> 02:18.263
[woman] Are you gonna
work here when you grow up?

02:18.763 --> 02:20.932
- Of course he will, it's named after him.
- What do you wanna be?

02:21.015 --> 02:24.936
[woman] Money's not gonna be a problem.
You're a lucky little boy. Bye!

02:26.771 --> 02:29.524
[Ho] That's it.
You hold your spoon just like this.

02:29.607 --> 02:32.068
And then, you get a good spoonful of rice.

02:32.152 --> 02:35.864
That's all you have to do,
eat well and be healthy. Okay? Like this.

02:36.656 --> 02:37.782
[Yeon-ok chuckles]

02:38.283 --> 02:40.076
- There. That's it.
- He's right.

02:40.160 --> 02:42.829
Don't worry about a thing,
just do whatever you want in life.

02:42.912 --> 02:45.373
Because that is all
we'll ever want from you, understand?

02:45.456 --> 02:47.417
- [Ho] Exactly.
- [parents gasping]

02:47.500 --> 02:49.377
- [Yeon-ok] Oh, my goodness. Wow.
- Good boy.

02:49.460 --> 02:52.714
[Ung] Some moments,
you don't have to do anything.

02:52.797 --> 02:54.382
Sometimes it's just the right choice.

02:55.174 --> 02:57.343
[both sobbing]

02:58.094 --> 03:02.265
Know your place in life. Especially
if it's borrowed from someone else.

03:04.267 --> 03:07.061
Ung, do you think you can draw Mommy?

03:07.645 --> 03:09.564
Ung, do you think
you can draw Daddy first?

03:09.647 --> 03:12.609
- [Yeon-ok] No. Ung--
- Ung, can you please draw Daddy first?

03:12.692 --> 03:16.154
- Pretty please? Come on.
- Oh, come on.

03:16.779 --> 03:18.364
[Ung] It's best not to be greedy…

03:18.448 --> 03:20.491
- you just can't be selfish.
- [Ho] I'm easier to draw.

03:24.746 --> 03:28.124
Ung, when are you ever gonna draw me, huh?

03:28.833 --> 03:31.669
Ung, when are you finally
gonna draw your Dad, huh?

03:32.211 --> 03:33.713
[Yeon-ok] Can you draw me, please?

03:33.796 --> 03:35.214
You know what? I'll draw you. I can!

03:35.298 --> 03:37.717
- What in the world do you know?
- Oh please. I'm a total natural.

03:37.800 --> 03:39.677
- Who do you think he takes after?
- [Yeon-ok] Me.

03:39.761 --> 03:43.306
Wow. That's a good pose. Hold on.
Good. Just stay still.

03:43.389 --> 03:46.476
Yep, that's a great angle.
You look beautiful. Let me do this.

03:47.393 --> 03:50.563
[Ung] That's why
I wanted to be a good son,

03:50.647 --> 03:52.774
at least one this perfect family deserved…

03:52.857 --> 03:54.734
[Ho] No, stop blinking.

03:55.526 --> 03:57.862
["Drawer" by 10CM playing]

03:59.989 --> 04:02.533
[Ung] …not the son
abandoned by his father.

04:02.617 --> 04:06.204
[Ho] Thanks to those groups of customers,
it's getting way too hectic in here.

04:06.871 --> 04:09.332
- Here you go.
- [Ho] Hectic nights, what a delight.

04:09.415 --> 04:12.085
[Ung] That means that,
if I don't do anything,

04:12.168 --> 04:13.544
maybe I'll turn out all right.

04:13.628 --> 04:16.673
[reporter] This one's come in just now.
A series of studies have established

04:16.756 --> 04:18.549
that one's genes
can have more of an effect

04:18.633 --> 04:20.426
towards determining one's personality,

04:20.510 --> 04:23.012
at least more than the environment
that a person is raised in.

04:23.513 --> 04:26.891
In order to support this theory,
gene-mapping researchers in the US,

04:26.975 --> 04:28.268
through a funded research,

04:28.351 --> 04:31.104
are currently looking for the genes
that are likely to determine one's per--

04:32.230 --> 04:34.941
- [Ho] Well, honestly, I don't know either.
- [Yeon-ok] Me neither.

04:37.277 --> 04:41.197
[Ung] Deep inside, I was afraid that I
might inherently be a worthless person.

04:43.491 --> 04:45.493
That's why I decided to play ignorant,

04:46.244 --> 04:48.413
pretending like I never cared all along.

04:49.664 --> 04:50.832
But in the end,

04:51.874 --> 04:53.918
I couldn't escape it after all.

04:56.296 --> 04:57.505
It's like fate.

04:58.631 --> 05:01.092
I ended up becoming
the person I was meant to be,

05:02.010 --> 05:06.222
worthless. Worthless man,
trapped in a worthless life.

05:06.306 --> 05:10.476
EPISODE 16
OUR BELOVED SUMMER

05:13.688 --> 05:17.817
ENROLLMENT GUIDE SCHOOL
OF ARCHITECTURE, ENSA, PARIS

05:22.905 --> 05:24.532
Yeon-su, I want you to come with me.

05:35.001 --> 05:36.544
I'm not taking this lightly at all.

05:38.254 --> 05:40.089
I've thought this through for a while.

05:41.132 --> 05:44.093
I know this all seems so sudden to you.

05:48.139 --> 05:50.099
Can you just trust me on this
and follow me?

05:57.565 --> 06:01.694
So this is something
you've been planning for a while now?

06:02.570 --> 06:05.281
I've been pathetic
the entire time since we met.

06:07.075 --> 06:08.242
That's why I thought…

06:09.702 --> 06:11.662
It's about time I start anew.

06:14.165 --> 06:15.249
However…

06:16.334 --> 06:17.418
I need you by my side.

06:18.836 --> 06:21.130
I can't do this on my own.

06:24.258 --> 06:27.178
But this… this means
you'll be going far away for a while--

06:27.261 --> 06:28.763
That doesn't matter. I need you.

06:28.846 --> 06:29.972
You know that.

06:34.268 --> 06:37.313
I'm asking you to come with me
and stay by my side through this.

06:43.152 --> 06:44.779
I know you know

06:45.696 --> 06:47.198
that I'm a huge mess.

06:51.077 --> 06:53.162
[soft gentle music]

06:58.251 --> 06:59.627
I'm gonna think about it.

07:00.711 --> 07:02.213
Give me some time first.

07:05.883 --> 07:08.261
It's something
I have to give some real thought.

07:08.803 --> 07:09.929
Really?

07:11.430 --> 07:12.390
Mm-hmm.

07:13.391 --> 07:16.894
I mean, after all, first time
you wanted to do something.

07:16.978 --> 07:19.063
[soft gentle music]

07:19.605 --> 07:20.857
[sighs]

07:21.399 --> 07:23.025
Bet I sounded more pathetic than usual.

07:23.985 --> 07:25.069
You didn't.

07:25.736 --> 07:28.656
And I never thought for once
that you were ever pathetic.

07:28.739 --> 07:31.242
You've achieved more than I have,
so shut it.

07:33.786 --> 07:36.164
[gentle music]

07:47.300 --> 07:50.094
Sorry? What did you just say?

07:52.597 --> 07:55.391
I said, I'd like for you to work
at our headquarters up in Paris.

07:56.309 --> 07:57.977
I've recently just been
assigned to go there

07:58.060 --> 07:59.770
and I need to assemble a new team for it.

07:59.854 --> 08:02.482
And you were
the first one I thought of who would fit.

08:02.565 --> 08:04.650
I looked through
all of the past projects you headed,

08:04.734 --> 08:06.527
and they were quite fascinating.

08:07.195 --> 08:08.446
Great. But why…

08:08.529 --> 08:10.907
You're someone that I need, Ms. Kook.
That's all there is to it.

08:13.075 --> 08:15.411
So once again,
I'd like you to come with me.

08:22.084 --> 08:23.961
You'll find the terms are quite favorable,

08:24.045 --> 08:25.588
along with the reason
I'm trying to recruit you.

08:25.671 --> 08:28.925
That is, because I know
how competent you are at this.

08:29.008 --> 08:29.842
[chuckles softly]

08:30.843 --> 08:32.094
Thank you very much.

08:32.678 --> 08:35.765
I didn't expect you of all people
to make an offer like this so…

08:36.557 --> 08:37.934
I'm not sure what to think.

08:38.518 --> 08:40.019
Am I still a sociopath to you?

08:40.102 --> 08:41.521
[chuckles]

08:42.063 --> 08:43.356
[Do-yul] That's all, I guess.

08:44.357 --> 08:46.275
Anyway, I need to take my dog for a walk.

08:46.359 --> 08:48.152
Give it some real thought and let me know.

09:05.211 --> 09:06.504
[I-hun] It's a good opportunity.

09:06.587 --> 09:10.424
Actually, Mr. Jang came to me first and
talked to me about it, before meeting you.

09:10.508 --> 09:13.761
He sure has a keen eye
for competent workers, I'll give him that.

09:13.844 --> 09:17.390
But anyway, don't ponder about it too much
and just say "Yes," understand?

09:17.473 --> 09:19.892
- I can't… I still--
- [I-hun] Yeon-su.

09:20.685 --> 09:24.230
Now listen, I'm saying this
as a friend who cares about you.

09:24.313 --> 09:26.524
I don't want you to miss this chance.
So take it.

09:27.233 --> 09:30.695
[I-hun] You've more than earned this.
I saw how hard you worked to get this far.

09:30.778 --> 09:33.197
So this time around,
put yourself first before anyone else

09:33.281 --> 09:34.865
and don't look back. Just try it.

09:34.949 --> 09:38.911
Also, this time,
try following your heart. Got it?

09:39.996 --> 09:41.914
[soft pensive music]

09:57.763 --> 09:59.557
How could he fire me just like that?

10:00.308 --> 10:02.685
I'm gonna file a complaint
for wrongful termination.

10:03.311 --> 10:05.146
I'm gonna expose
everything wrong that he's done

10:05.229 --> 10:08.190
and then I'm gonna sue his ass to death.

10:08.274 --> 10:10.568
You're not going to do any of that.

10:10.651 --> 10:12.612
[sniffling]
Choi Ung, you dirty scumbag.

10:12.695 --> 10:14.614
[Eun-ho] That guy
can't do anything without my help.

10:14.697 --> 10:16.741
So let's see
how well he does from here on.

10:16.824 --> 10:18.826
What can you do though?
He really wants to go.

10:19.744 --> 10:22.246
If you're really that sad,
just tag along with him.

10:22.330 --> 10:24.790
Can you believe
he didn't even bother inviting me to go?

10:25.583 --> 10:27.001
He could have at least tried asking.

10:27.084 --> 10:29.545
And then I would have reluctantly
given in eventually.

10:30.212 --> 10:31.922
I can't believe him. Why?

10:33.633 --> 10:35.384
What would you even
do in France if you go?

10:35.968 --> 10:37.178
If he's gonna go there to study,

10:37.261 --> 10:39.889
why would he ask you to tag along?
He made the decision for your sake.

10:39.972 --> 10:43.017
No, look. He told me to live my life.
The nerve of that guy.

10:43.100 --> 10:45.770
Exactly whose life does he think
I've been living for all this time?

10:46.437 --> 10:49.565
What does he think? That I can't do
anything without him to order me around?

10:50.650 --> 10:52.735
What are you gonna do without him?

10:53.235 --> 10:54.278
Well, obviously…

10:56.155 --> 10:57.156
I can do…

10:58.783 --> 11:01.369
[sobbing]
I can't do anything without him. Oh, God…

11:02.536 --> 11:04.622
[sobbing dramatically]

11:07.833 --> 11:08.834
DAEHAN BANK

11:09.418 --> 11:11.253
Okay, now what?

11:14.423 --> 11:15.424
[gasping shout]

11:16.258 --> 11:17.426
[Sol-i] Wait!

11:17.927 --> 11:19.637
Hey, tell me. What is it?

11:19.720 --> 11:20.596
Come on.

11:20.679 --> 11:22.473
[sobbing loudly]

11:23.766 --> 11:26.644
- [Sol-i] What are these? Tears or snot?
- My severance pay…

11:26.727 --> 11:28.104
Your nose is running like crazy.

11:28.187 --> 11:30.231
- It's my severance pay…
- It's your what?

11:30.314 --> 11:31.649
- My severance pay…
- What about it?

11:31.732 --> 11:33.234
Is he not giving you any?

11:33.317 --> 11:35.236
He gave me way too much…

11:36.070 --> 11:38.072
- [cheeky music]
- [dramatic sobbing]

11:44.745 --> 11:45.830
[gasping shout]

11:46.705 --> 11:47.706
[Sol-i] No way!

11:49.500 --> 11:50.793
[Eun-ho crying]

11:56.298 --> 11:57.466
Eun-ho.

11:58.008 --> 11:59.885
If you don't have any plans,

12:00.386 --> 12:03.931
like in the future, what do you say
if we… start a business together?

12:04.682 --> 12:06.809
[suddenly stops crying]
Don't be absurd, Sol-i.

12:06.892 --> 12:08.394
I don't do business with others.

12:12.481 --> 12:14.525
Seeing as I already got a friend discount,

12:15.734 --> 12:17.695
how about a celebrity discount?

12:18.279 --> 12:20.281
I'll give you
a bigger discount if you want.

12:20.364 --> 12:21.407
I was just kidding.

12:21.490 --> 12:24.410
You should stop saying things that
can devalue your work. It's not right.

12:24.994 --> 12:26.996
Impossible.
They aren't even that great to begin with.

12:29.748 --> 12:32.918
Wait. So by extension
are you trying to say

12:33.002 --> 12:34.962
that I probably
have terrible taste in art?

12:35.045 --> 12:36.630
Nah-uh, not what I meant.

12:36.714 --> 12:39.300
Do you wanna know the reason
why I like your drawings?

12:40.301 --> 12:42.970
The more I looked at them,
the more I realize

12:43.053 --> 12:46.348
why your drawings always gave me
the feeling of comfort.

12:46.432 --> 12:49.351
Those crooked lines
let off more than you realize.

12:49.977 --> 12:54.106
[NJ] They made me wonder if by chance
you were just as insecure as I was.

12:55.107 --> 12:57.776
Your stubbornness
to only draw unchangeable objects,

12:58.611 --> 13:02.448
deep down I always wondered
if perhaps you were just as lonely as me.

13:04.533 --> 13:07.661
But then I look at your final work,
it all just comes together.

13:08.829 --> 13:10.372
It gives me this warm feeling.

13:11.415 --> 13:12.666
It looks stable.

13:14.126 --> 13:16.587
As if it was drawn by…

13:18.088 --> 13:20.466
someone a lot more resilient than others.

13:24.011 --> 13:26.180
Surprisingly, that comforts me.

13:27.723 --> 13:30.309
It's as if you're telling me
that I can become just like you.

13:34.897 --> 13:38.734
That's it. That's basically
my critique of your work.

13:39.818 --> 13:42.696
So don't mind the others
and listen to someone who understands.

13:42.780 --> 13:44.281
After all, I'm your biggest buyer.

13:45.449 --> 13:46.617
I appreciate it.

13:47.243 --> 13:49.745
You know,
somehow it's actually very comforting.

13:51.747 --> 13:54.333
I just realized
how close we've already become

13:54.416 --> 13:56.293
seeing how we've been
comforting each other.

13:56.377 --> 13:57.670
[both chuckle]

14:00.464 --> 14:04.176
So anyway,
I'm quite sad to be saying goodbye.

14:04.760 --> 14:07.346
Studying abroad
makes you feel really lonely.

14:07.429 --> 14:09.723
I'll be fine. Yeon-su's coming along.

14:12.560 --> 14:13.769
Oh, really?

14:14.270 --> 14:16.355
Should be obvious
that I can't live without her.

14:16.438 --> 14:17.273
Oh.

14:18.816 --> 14:20.401
You're a lucky guy.

14:22.194 --> 14:24.655
That just proves
how much she really loves you.

14:25.906 --> 14:27.449
[NJ] She chose your life over hers.

14:27.533 --> 14:30.202
Not an easy thing,
dedicating yourself to someone.

14:31.328 --> 14:33.455
That's quite the sacrifice she's making.

14:44.383 --> 14:45.467
Grandma.

14:46.510 --> 14:47.678
Hmm?

14:48.679 --> 14:51.015
Are you really going to be okay
without me here?

14:51.098 --> 14:53.475
Of course. I'll be just fine.

14:54.602 --> 14:56.645
Wow, you didn't even think about that.

14:57.146 --> 14:58.522
That kinda hurts.

14:59.940 --> 15:04.486
My life's simple. I'll be busy
spending time with my old friends.

15:04.570 --> 15:08.240
I know, but what if you collapse again
and no one's around to help you?

15:08.324 --> 15:12.912
As long as I take my blood pressure meds
regularly, they said I'd be fine.

15:12.995 --> 15:14.163
Oof.

15:16.081 --> 15:18.584
I'm fine. Just go.

15:18.667 --> 15:22.963
And stop worrying about me.
You follow your heart for a change.

15:26.675 --> 15:29.053
Think of it as a favor. You got that?

15:33.057 --> 15:34.975
Come on. Let's go.

15:35.059 --> 15:37.770
Goodness. Let's go.

15:37.853 --> 15:39.813
[gentle music]

15:43.192 --> 15:44.735
[NJ] She chose your life over hers.

15:44.818 --> 15:47.363
Not an easy thing,
dedicating yourself to someone.

15:47.988 --> 15:51.408
I mean, after all, first time
you wanted to do something.

15:52.534 --> 15:54.578
[gentle pensive music]

15:54.662 --> 15:55.829
[sighs]

16:28.487 --> 16:32.074
Also, this time,
try following your heart. Got it?

16:33.534 --> 16:36.745
I'm fine. And stop worrying about me.

16:36.829 --> 16:38.580
You follow your heart for a change.

16:40.666 --> 16:43.002
I should start following my heart?

16:45.254 --> 16:47.256
[gentle pensive music]

16:57.725 --> 17:04.440
DAILY BEER

17:12.531 --> 17:14.616
- [Dong-il] Thank you very much.
- My pleasure, sir.

17:21.749 --> 17:22.624
Do it.

17:23.876 --> 17:25.669
I can't think of
a single reason why I should.

17:25.753 --> 17:27.546
Because that's exactly what we do.

17:28.380 --> 17:30.507
Recording these moments in people's lives.

17:31.341 --> 17:33.927
We're always explaining
how priceless that is.

17:34.011 --> 17:36.889
Part of our job is to convince them
how important those memories are.

17:36.972 --> 17:37.890
So what makes you so different?

17:37.973 --> 17:40.559
The difference is,
there's nothing worth recording.

17:45.898 --> 17:46.940
[Ji-ung] You know what?

17:48.400 --> 17:49.526
I just don't get it.

17:51.028 --> 17:54.281
My ghost of a mom suddenly comes back
out of nowhere, saying that she's dying.

17:54.865 --> 17:56.283
And now she wants me to film her.

17:57.117 --> 18:00.037
Why now? What am I supposed to do?

18:01.455 --> 18:03.290
Why should I even consider…

18:05.167 --> 18:07.169
What makes her think I'd do it for her?

18:09.671 --> 18:11.548
After all this time, why would I do that?

18:12.549 --> 18:14.134
Simple, you do it for yourself.

18:16.762 --> 18:18.972
You're the one who has to live with it.

18:19.056 --> 18:21.600
Someone has to be able
to carry that memory forward,

18:21.683 --> 18:23.227
so that it doesn't fade away.

18:24.144 --> 18:25.479
You don't do it, no one else will.

18:31.568 --> 18:32.402
[Ji-ung sighs]

18:33.153 --> 18:34.238
Hey.

18:34.947 --> 18:37.783
Do you even have a portrait of her
you can use for her funeral?

18:41.328 --> 18:42.412
Funny, right?

18:43.288 --> 18:44.915
Your job is to film other people,

18:44.998 --> 18:47.417
yet you don't have
a single photo of your mom.

18:48.836 --> 18:52.047
I didn't have any photos of my mom either,
except for this one.

18:52.131 --> 18:55.008
It was some group photo
with people I don't know.

18:56.260 --> 18:59.930
She was surrounded by all these
other people and smiling from ear to ear.

19:02.432 --> 19:05.018
But I'm grateful,
because at least I have that.

19:05.978 --> 19:08.647
I look at it every now and then,
when I think about her.

19:09.648 --> 19:11.525
[soft emotional music]

19:16.071 --> 19:19.575
Regardless, I don't know
the entire story between you and your mom.

19:19.658 --> 19:23.787
You can resent her or you can forgive her,
but that can wait for now.

19:23.871 --> 19:27.541
Someone is dying.
Someone you clearly think about.

19:27.624 --> 19:29.751
[Dong-il] Don't waste this moment
by doing nothing.

19:32.296 --> 19:33.297
That's all.

19:35.382 --> 19:37.050
[soft emotional music]

20:26.475 --> 20:28.185
- Ung.
- Hmm?

20:29.228 --> 20:30.938
I was thinking this evening…

20:32.564 --> 20:34.483
do you wanna go to Sol-i's later?

20:36.902 --> 20:37.986
Okay.

20:44.576 --> 20:46.536
[gentle music]

20:59.591 --> 21:01.385
Okay. I understand.

21:01.885 --> 21:03.845
And I respect your decision.

21:14.064 --> 21:15.148
[puffs out breath]

21:18.318 --> 21:19.319
Oh, come on.

21:19.403 --> 21:22.614
The owner of this restaurant
sure makes her customers uncomfortable.

21:22.698 --> 21:25.617
Well, only for this one specific customer,

21:25.701 --> 21:28.245
since he's so busy, he rarely visits us.

21:28.328 --> 21:29.830
[both chuckle]

21:29.913 --> 21:33.458
You must be busy with your girlfriend,
so what brings you all the way over here?

21:34.334 --> 21:37.129
No reason.
I just missed your food, that's all.

21:42.926 --> 21:44.761
Oh. I'm not a kid anymore.

21:51.977 --> 21:55.105
You should eat well
whenever something's worrying you.

21:55.188 --> 21:57.107
I never said I was worried.

21:57.190 --> 21:59.276
You don't have to. I'm your mom.

22:08.076 --> 22:09.911
Oh, my little son.

22:10.662 --> 22:12.748
I can't believe you're all grown up.

22:34.644 --> 22:36.188
You knew all along…

22:37.314 --> 22:38.356
Hmm.

22:39.024 --> 22:40.692
Of course I knew.

22:43.070 --> 22:44.613
…that I knew about it?

22:53.080 --> 22:56.333
After… did that change anything?

22:57.584 --> 22:59.586
Why would that change anything?

22:59.669 --> 23:02.714
It's irrelevant.
You're my son no matter what happens.

23:06.510 --> 23:12.265
I've been blessed. And I knew right away,
you've always been my son, Ung.

23:17.854 --> 23:19.606
Thank you for being my son.

23:20.148 --> 23:24.861
I'm so grateful
seeing you grow up into a wonderful man.

23:33.578 --> 23:34.663
I…

23:40.836 --> 23:42.546
I was afraid…

23:45.006 --> 23:47.259
that I wouldn't take after you and Dad.

23:48.426 --> 23:50.554
[breathing shakily]

23:51.138 --> 23:53.098
[emotional vulnerable music]

23:56.601 --> 24:00.105
I was afraid I wouldn't turn out
to be a good person like you.

24:05.318 --> 24:07.320
I was hoping I'd become good enough…

24:10.073 --> 24:11.825
at least good enough in your eyes.

24:13.451 --> 24:15.203
[Ung] I was so scared that I would…

24:16.079 --> 24:17.789
end up disappointing you.

24:19.374 --> 24:21.042
That's what I'm most afraid of.

24:22.210 --> 24:23.461
[sighs]

24:24.588 --> 24:26.131
What can I say, Ung?

24:27.257 --> 24:31.261
Your dad and I,
we were never disappointed in you.

24:32.345 --> 24:33.847
[sniffles]

24:34.806 --> 24:39.144
Ever since the moment we saw you
and embraced you in our arms,

24:40.270 --> 24:43.064
we have loved every single part of you.

24:43.773 --> 24:45.775
[emotional vulnerable music]

24:56.119 --> 24:57.871
[both chuckling]

25:05.670 --> 25:06.755
Mom.

25:06.838 --> 25:08.006
Yes?

25:08.089 --> 25:09.216
[Ung] Right now,

25:09.925 --> 25:12.344
I just wanna become
a better version of myself.

25:13.136 --> 25:15.305
You know, all I wish is that…

25:16.932 --> 25:20.477
you will at least be able
to get some good sleep now.

25:26.608 --> 25:27.525
[chuckles]

25:27.609 --> 25:30.862
Hurry and eat your food. You're gonna
miss out if you let it go cold.

25:36.493 --> 25:39.037
[producer] NJ, congratulations,
this is your last interview.

25:40.038 --> 25:42.999
We've prepared the questions right here.
We made a copy for you.

25:43.083 --> 25:45.377
You can go through them and check,
in case you wanna make sure.

25:45.460 --> 25:49.214
First question there, we were wondering
if there was a specific reason you

25:49.297 --> 25:52.217
chose this place to shoot for
your last interview. All right keep it up.

25:52.801 --> 25:55.720
Excuse me, sir,
I have a small favor to ask you.

25:55.804 --> 25:57.013
Sure.

25:57.514 --> 25:58.515
What is it?

26:05.272 --> 26:06.273
[sighs softly]

26:11.611 --> 26:14.739
- Oh, have you been here long?
- No, not really.

26:16.449 --> 26:18.076
[Yeon-su] Really cold out there.

26:18.159 --> 26:19.411
Yeah, it's freezing.

26:20.495 --> 26:21.329
[groans]

26:21.413 --> 26:23.581
I told you
to wear thicker clothes, didn't I?

26:24.082 --> 26:25.792
I warmed up my hands for you.

26:26.668 --> 26:27.919
- Can you feel it?
- Hmm.

26:28.545 --> 26:31.339
But I'm really fine.
You'll get cold again.

26:31.923 --> 26:32.924
That's okay.

26:40.181 --> 26:41.641
Have you…

26:42.767 --> 26:44.060
made up your mind?

26:45.520 --> 26:46.521
Hmm.

26:49.858 --> 26:51.234
[sighs]

26:52.152 --> 26:54.237
[gentle music]

27:12.297 --> 27:16.051
I knew it. You're always waiting.

27:19.137 --> 27:21.222
[gentle music]

27:24.225 --> 27:25.101
[Yeon-su groans]

27:43.787 --> 27:44.954
Grandma.

27:49.250 --> 27:51.294
Do you remember what you told me?

27:54.005 --> 27:56.800
That I should stop
enduring everything on my own.

27:58.635 --> 28:00.970
To go out there and make friends,

28:02.263 --> 28:04.140
follow what my heart wants,

28:05.016 --> 28:06.476
and just enjoy life.

28:09.437 --> 28:11.564
So this time around I'm…

28:12.816 --> 28:14.984
I'm going to make the bold choice

28:16.361 --> 28:18.696
and follow what my heart's wanted
all along.

28:22.075 --> 28:24.327
[Yeon-su] And do you know what I realized?

28:25.745 --> 28:28.456
That all this time,
that's how I've been living.

28:31.835 --> 28:35.046
I have no idea
where I got the notion that I was alone.

28:38.007 --> 28:39.217
Honestly…

28:42.011 --> 28:44.431
there was never a time when I was alone.

28:56.526 --> 28:59.404
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim playing]

29:06.494 --> 29:08.246
Hey. I'm here!

29:08.913 --> 29:10.290
- Welcome to…
- Hey!

29:12.459 --> 29:13.293
Hey…

29:13.376 --> 29:16.421
[Sol-i] Hey, I came up with a scenario.
Give me an objective review.

29:16.504 --> 29:17.922
I've been writing this for a while…

29:18.006 --> 29:19.799
What do I do?
He asked for my number in public.

29:19.883 --> 29:21.760
The title is Point of Omniscient Psycho…

29:21.843 --> 29:24.220
…he looked pretty sincere, too.
What do you think? Should I go for it?

29:24.804 --> 29:27.640
I have an offer and I want you
to think about it carefully.

29:27.724 --> 29:30.393
I-hun, I'm a little too busy.
I can't make--

29:30.477 --> 29:31.978
Work with me. I wanna hire you.

29:33.646 --> 29:35.523
I'm sorry, like I said,
I'm a little too busy.

29:35.607 --> 29:37.400
I'm not just
asking for your help, Yeon-su.

29:37.484 --> 29:39.527
I am recruiting you, as in officially.

29:41.029 --> 29:43.865
It's a business that I'm starting
and the terms aren't so bad.

29:45.325 --> 29:49.078
Right. Also, you get a signing bonus.
[chuckles]

29:51.706 --> 29:55.084
Just a sec. I never asked for your help,
why the sudden offer?

29:55.835 --> 30:00.173
'Cause I know that eventually
you'll land a job at a big company,

30:00.256 --> 30:01.925
only a matter of time, really.

30:02.008 --> 30:03.718
[I-hun] I know that my company is small.

30:03.802 --> 30:06.137
But you're going to be getting
a lot of work done,

30:06.221 --> 30:08.181
I'll be getting my money's worth for sure.

30:08.264 --> 30:09.599
I'm saying…

30:10.183 --> 30:12.769
this will be the biggest investment
that I've ever made,

30:12.852 --> 30:14.395
but I know that it's worth it.

30:15.647 --> 30:17.440
So just read all this through.

30:18.024 --> 30:20.735
If you change your mind,
just call me. Okay?

30:21.319 --> 30:23.446
Oh. Thanks for the coffee.

30:25.198 --> 30:27.492
["Summer Rain" softly playing]

30:36.042 --> 30:38.253
CONTRACT
RUN AND GOOK YEON-SU'S AGREEMENT

30:40.630 --> 30:41.965
RUN, SINSAMALL
ON AND OFFLINE PR PLANS

30:50.390 --> 30:51.432
- [I-hun] Yeon-su.
- Yeah?

30:51.516 --> 30:55.270
Can you include this part right here?
It's important that we put that in there.

30:55.353 --> 30:56.521
You got it? Okay?

30:56.604 --> 30:59.148
We need to collaborate.
We need to communicate more.

30:59.232 --> 31:00.525
RUN
COMMUNICATION GROUP

31:00.608 --> 31:01.651
[Ye-in] Ms. Kook!

31:02.151 --> 31:04.779
Hey, Ms. Kook!
Your presentation was awesome. Oh, my God!

31:04.863 --> 31:06.281
It was such a clean-cut
and direct presentation.

31:06.865 --> 31:09.242
I think we got this in the bag,
I can tell! You're the best!

31:09.742 --> 31:10.910
[I-hun] I'm not even surprised anymore.

31:10.994 --> 31:14.372
Seriously, when are you gonna stop
getting better? Do you even have a limit?

31:14.455 --> 31:16.291
[all laughing happily]

31:16.875 --> 31:18.918
Am I right? She never stops!
Just keeps setting the bar.

31:19.419 --> 31:20.837
- Get-together tonight?
- Sure thing!

31:21.337 --> 31:22.630
[laughing and cheering]

31:22.714 --> 31:25.258
[Yeon-su] I thought
my life was pretty dull for some reason.

31:31.973 --> 31:34.642
But I have so many good memories.

31:35.602 --> 31:37.437
I never realized.

31:38.855 --> 31:41.566
The only one
who made my life seem pathetic…

31:44.402 --> 31:46.279
it was me all along.

31:47.989 --> 31:49.157
Grandma.

31:50.950 --> 31:54.245
["Summer Rain" continuing]

31:57.665 --> 31:59.250
[sighs]

32:10.929 --> 32:12.096
I'm not going,

32:13.306 --> 32:14.223
Ung.

32:19.771 --> 32:21.439
For the first time,

32:22.440 --> 32:24.943
I'm finally beginning to enjoy my life.

32:25.944 --> 32:27.320
For the first time,

32:28.029 --> 32:30.406
I can clearly see the path I took.

32:31.991 --> 32:35.286
That's why
I wanna live this life a bit longer.

32:38.498 --> 32:40.124
I used to think that

32:41.584 --> 32:46.005
I had no option
but to push on with this life I was given.

32:48.007 --> 32:49.342
But now…

32:50.969 --> 32:53.638
I think this was the life
I wanted in the first place.

32:55.598 --> 32:56.683
That's why…

32:58.226 --> 33:01.521
I wanna live my life
with no regrets and keep going.

33:10.279 --> 33:11.948
Say something, will you?

33:14.951 --> 33:17.036
I was thinking about how long it'd take.

33:19.372 --> 33:20.665
For what?

33:22.125 --> 33:24.752
The time it'll take
for me to earn what I really want.

33:26.254 --> 33:28.631
How long it'd take for me to deserve you.

33:30.758 --> 33:32.635
What do you mean, deserve me?

33:33.803 --> 33:36.931
You're an exceptional person, Yeon-su.
You're way beyond my league.

33:38.725 --> 33:39.976
But me…

33:41.853 --> 33:43.938
I've just been wasting way too much time.

33:46.190 --> 33:47.400
But you know what?

33:49.610 --> 33:52.113
I've finally realized
what it is I need to do.

33:53.322 --> 33:55.283
What I really wanted to do,

33:56.034 --> 33:58.119
what I desire most of all.

34:00.830 --> 34:02.665
I know who I am now.

34:02.749 --> 34:05.251
[gentle music]

34:09.297 --> 34:10.590
And that's why…

34:11.883 --> 34:13.051
I think…

34:15.386 --> 34:17.180
It's okay, Ung.

34:18.014 --> 34:20.224
[gentle music]

34:30.568 --> 34:31.736
You can go.

34:32.945 --> 34:34.489
Everyone's gonna be okay.

34:37.366 --> 34:39.285
[soft sweet music]

34:43.539 --> 34:45.333
I promise, it won't take too long.

34:47.126 --> 34:48.127
Hmm.

34:49.128 --> 34:50.797
I'm not gonna change either.

34:53.633 --> 34:54.842
Hmm.

34:56.928 --> 34:58.721
I will come back, I swear.

35:02.058 --> 35:03.142
Hmm.

35:05.603 --> 35:07.146
So please, just…

35:10.191 --> 35:11.859
I'm asking you to wait for me.

35:14.362 --> 35:16.239
[soft sweet music]

35:55.194 --> 35:56.737
Why are you just standing there?

35:56.821 --> 35:58.656
Come over here and sit down.

36:00.491 --> 36:03.119
We were always so distant,
so I'm fine over here.

36:04.203 --> 36:07.039
How can you suddenly think
it's okay to approach me now?

36:09.917 --> 36:11.169
It's unfair…

36:14.005 --> 36:16.465
to just die like this all alone.

36:17.091 --> 36:20.136
If I died
without even leaving a single trace…

36:21.345 --> 36:23.139
that I ever existed…

36:23.931 --> 36:25.016
that's just unfair.

36:28.102 --> 36:29.312
You're selfish

36:30.605 --> 36:32.273
just like you've always been.

36:34.400 --> 36:35.651
That's what I'll be…

36:40.281 --> 36:42.658
horrible until the day I die.

36:42.742 --> 36:46.162
[Ji-ung's mom] I understand.
You don't have to care about me.

36:46.245 --> 36:50.333
Maybe it's okay to feel a little sorry

36:50.833 --> 36:52.168
just a little…

36:54.295 --> 36:55.796
and pay a visit

36:56.923 --> 36:58.674
from time to time.

36:58.758 --> 36:59.592
[mild scoff]

37:00.343 --> 37:01.177
[breathes in sharply]

37:18.903 --> 37:20.613
[Ji-ung] It doesn't make any sense.

37:21.530 --> 37:24.033
Why would you even come back
if that's what you wanted?

37:25.159 --> 37:27.203
You want things to be just the same?

37:27.286 --> 37:29.538
You should've never
showed your face again.

37:33.417 --> 37:34.752
[soft shaky breath]

37:37.213 --> 37:38.923
Can you please say something?

37:41.759 --> 37:42.927
Say something.

37:45.221 --> 37:46.472
Anything.

37:54.772 --> 37:56.023
[Ji-ung's mom] Back then…

37:58.651 --> 38:02.154
I couldn't handle it,
the sickness I had in my heart.

38:02.238 --> 38:04.573
I didn't have a choice, I just didn't.

38:06.284 --> 38:07.785
I was afraid that

38:08.661 --> 38:14.333
eventually, being with you…
you'd be just as miserable.

38:15.876 --> 38:17.128
At times…

38:20.089 --> 38:22.133
I would see your face out there…

38:23.843 --> 38:25.845
so bright and full of life.

38:28.806 --> 38:30.850
And the thing I feared the most…

38:32.810 --> 38:35.479
was that I'd ruin you
and drag you down with me.

38:35.563 --> 38:36.397
[sobs]

38:36.897 --> 38:38.983
I was so scared. That's why…

38:40.651 --> 38:43.946
That's why I couldn't…
I couldn't bear embrace you.

38:45.072 --> 38:47.658
["Home" by Janet Suhh playing]

38:51.662 --> 38:53.414
I not going to forgive you.

38:54.915 --> 38:56.125
I can't.

38:58.377 --> 38:59.545
Not ever.

39:02.089 --> 39:03.174
I know.

39:04.508 --> 39:06.344
The suffering you're going through…

39:10.014 --> 39:12.266
can never justify what you did to me.

39:14.935 --> 39:15.936
I know.

39:17.313 --> 39:18.314
All right?

39:20.483 --> 39:21.942
You were a mother.

39:26.697 --> 39:27.573
And me…

39:30.159 --> 39:31.744
I was just a little kid.

39:33.496 --> 39:35.998
[Ji-ung] How could a mother
do that to her own son?

39:38.626 --> 39:39.835
You're right.

39:39.919 --> 39:43.756
How could you suddenly just appear
and tell me that you're dying?

39:48.969 --> 39:52.264
[Ji-ung] You hurt me.
I'll never forgive you.

39:54.600 --> 39:55.935
It's not gonna happen.

39:57.478 --> 39:58.813
[crying softly]
Okay.

40:01.273 --> 40:02.483
But maybe…

40:04.693 --> 40:06.487
who knows, one of these days…

40:08.989 --> 40:10.950
I might just
change my mind out of nowhere.

40:12.910 --> 40:14.120
[Ji-ung] So please just…

40:17.748 --> 40:19.333
I want you to fight to live.

40:21.752 --> 40:25.673
Better now than never,
you and I can start with a clean slate.

40:26.424 --> 40:28.968
We don't have to keep relying
on other people anymore.

40:31.929 --> 40:34.098
Let's just live an ordinary life together…

40:36.350 --> 40:37.852
you know, like everyone else.

40:38.853 --> 40:40.646
["Home" playing]

40:54.410 --> 40:57.204
[Ung] We were 29 years old. Headstrong.

40:57.997 --> 41:00.374
That was the time
we all took charge of our lives.

41:03.252 --> 41:06.839
And then, I had to get ready
to leave for abroad.

41:08.507 --> 41:09.675
[sighs]

41:10.384 --> 41:11.844
I told my parents right away too.

41:11.927 --> 41:13.929
By the end of the month, I'll be leaving.

41:14.013 --> 41:15.806
[Ho breathes angrily]

41:16.390 --> 41:17.892
[Yeon-ok] Honey.

41:18.559 --> 41:21.812
[Ung] Surprisingly,
my dad got really upset

41:21.896 --> 41:23.230
and refused to see me for a month.

41:23.314 --> 41:26.150
Come on, he always nagged me
when I was around.

41:32.448 --> 41:33.616
[email beeping]

41:34.658 --> 41:36.285
YOU'VE LEFT ME,
BUT I'M SENDING THIS FOR YOU

41:36.368 --> 41:38.329
Eun-ho was also mad at me.

41:38.412 --> 41:41.540
And he sent me a 60-page document
on how to survive.

41:42.625 --> 41:45.586
Oh, Ji-ung has also been very busy.

41:45.669 --> 41:47.588
He's being filmed now, ironically.

41:47.671 --> 41:49.173
I'm… uhm…

41:50.174 --> 41:51.175
[Ji-ung] So I was…

41:53.093 --> 41:54.595
I'm sorry.
Can you repeat the question again?

41:54.678 --> 41:57.056
I was asking you to please share with us

41:57.139 --> 42:00.226
some of the most memorable moments
you've had with her, Mr. Kim.

42:00.726 --> 42:01.810
All right.

42:02.394 --> 42:03.687
Cue.

42:03.771 --> 42:05.397
[Ji-ung] Most memorable, huh?

42:05.481 --> 42:08.734
Oh. I think
every last Saturday of the month…

42:10.402 --> 42:13.572
we'd go to the marketplace
every afternoon and have some tteokbokki.

42:14.156 --> 42:18.452
I remember my mom was always busy.
That was the only day she had off.

42:18.536 --> 42:19.370
[chuckles softly]

42:20.412 --> 42:23.290
We'd go to the market,
hold hands and walk around.

42:23.958 --> 42:25.918
It made me happy, doing that.

42:26.502 --> 42:29.588
[Ung] Well, the guy who always
talked about being an observer,

42:29.672 --> 42:32.299
finally knows what it's like
to be on the other side.

42:35.052 --> 42:37.805
[NJ] You've all seen me from the surface
but I hope that you're not forgetting…

42:37.888 --> 42:39.807
[Ung] Oh, NJ, as usual,

42:39.890 --> 42:42.226
is causing her agency even more headaches.

42:42.810 --> 42:46.063
 Being in front of a camera, I always
wanted to show you my cheerful side.

42:46.146 --> 42:48.607
[Ung] A 30-minute no hold barred,
unedited footage

42:48.691 --> 42:50.401
broadcasted
out of the blue with no warning.

42:50.484 --> 42:52.319
So please be kind to one another.

42:54.113 --> 42:56.657
[Ung] The public seems
to be bashing her once again,

42:56.740 --> 42:59.326
but now she's also receiving
just as much support.

43:00.244 --> 43:01.912
As for Yeon-su and myself…

43:01.996 --> 43:03.080
[Yeon-su] Ung.

43:07.793 --> 43:09.545
[laughs]

43:10.713 --> 43:12.089
- Did you get cold?
- Nope.

43:12.172 --> 43:14.216
- Were you waiting for a while?
- Not even.

43:14.300 --> 43:15.634
Let's go.

43:15.718 --> 43:17.595
[Ung] We made the best
of our time together.

43:18.554 --> 43:21.348
["Red String Of Fate"
by Kim Kyung Hee playing]

43:29.732 --> 43:31.191
[both chuckling]

43:32.776 --> 43:35.112
Just us, every single day.

43:35.195 --> 43:38.407
Tell me, did you really rehearse
spraying me with water every day?

43:38.490 --> 43:41.910
Originally, I was going to pour
a bucket over you, so you got lucky.

43:41.994 --> 43:43.245
Unless you dump me again.

43:44.038 --> 43:46.290
Now I'm really curious
if you'd really do it.

43:46.874 --> 43:49.793
No. I take that back.
And enough of that. Don't do it again.

43:49.877 --> 43:51.086
No more what-ifs and stuff.

43:52.212 --> 43:54.798
Okay, I promise. But can I ask you
one last what-if question?

43:54.882 --> 43:56.342
- No!
- What if we…

43:56.967 --> 43:58.302
[laughing]

43:58.886 --> 44:00.346
- [Ung] Every single day.
- What if we suddenly…

44:00.429 --> 44:01.847
- [Ung] Stop it!
- [Yeon-su laughing]

44:03.474 --> 44:05.726
["Red String Of Fate" continuing]

44:21.742 --> 44:22.993
[Ung] It was perfect.

44:24.578 --> 44:27.998
However, I had to go.
The day of my flight came pretty quick.

44:28.082 --> 44:29.541
Oh, my God, Ung, we're screwed!

44:29.625 --> 44:31.919
- [Ung] What? What is it?
- This is bad. I'm telling you.

44:32.002 --> 44:33.629
- This is a disaster, Ung.
- [Ung] What?

44:34.546 --> 44:36.548
- What's wrong?
- Our tank is low.

44:37.174 --> 44:39.301
[Ho] And we're gonna be late
if we have to stop for gas.

44:39.385 --> 44:41.470
You can't be late for your flight,
they'd leave without you,

44:41.553 --> 44:43.389
- so how about you just don't go?
- Come on, Dad.

44:43.472 --> 44:45.474
I can see you've got a full tank,
which is rare.

44:45.557 --> 44:47.309
Plus, we have some time to spare.

44:47.393 --> 44:48.477
[sighs]

44:50.062 --> 44:53.649
Right. I almost forgot,
I have to stop by somewhere.

44:53.732 --> 44:54.983
[Ung] Wait for me outside.

44:55.067 --> 44:58.070
Hey, Son. Go wherever
you need to go. Don't come back.

44:58.153 --> 45:00.114
Don't come back
so you can miss the flight.

45:00.197 --> 45:01.615
I'll say there was an accident, huh?

45:02.699 --> 45:03.742
Not gonna take long.

45:06.995 --> 45:11.208
[Ung] There was one more thing I had to do
before I could embark on my new journey.

45:16.004 --> 45:18.507
I had to finally confront the past…

45:19.716 --> 45:21.301
the one that had haunted me.

45:32.229 --> 45:34.523
I wanted to just tell him
once and for all…

45:35.899 --> 45:38.235
there's no need to keep hurting himself,

45:38.318 --> 45:40.571
there's no more need to avoid me,

45:40.654 --> 45:42.531
or feel sorry for ourselves.

45:43.115 --> 45:45.451
[soft music]

45:48.620 --> 45:50.247
We've done that more than enough,

45:51.957 --> 45:54.209
it's time for us to let go of each other.

46:03.927 --> 46:07.764
[Yeon-su] And just like that,
Ung had left around the end of winter.

46:12.978 --> 46:14.855
I was fine. Same as usual.

46:15.439 --> 46:18.317
You see, I'm a lot more mature
when it comes to relationships.

46:18.817 --> 46:22.779
Where are you, my little Ung? My baby Ung.

46:22.863 --> 46:25.199
I miss you so much…

46:25.282 --> 46:27.534
I'm begging you,
can someone please call the cops?

46:28.118 --> 46:30.996
I want this psycho behind bars,
she's scaring off all my customers.

46:31.079 --> 46:34.583
[screaming]
Ung! Where are you?

46:34.666 --> 46:37.085
- [Yeon-su] Of course, naturally…
- Someone find my Ung!

46:37.169 --> 46:40.547
[Yeon-su] …there were a few little days
when I missed him a bit too much.

46:43.342 --> 46:45.886
What if a female student
who lives right next to you,

46:45.969 --> 46:47.429
knocks on your door, you answer,

46:47.513 --> 46:51.433
then she asks for butter
or whatever it is they use as an excuse.

46:51.517 --> 46:53.519
I'm gonna lock the door
and then call the police.

46:53.602 --> 46:55.938
Good answer.
[chuckles]

46:56.021 --> 46:57.773
Okay, what if something else happened.

46:57.856 --> 47:00.067
You're busy somewhere studying
and a female student

47:00.150 --> 47:02.778
tells you she speaks Korean
and offers to teach you French.

47:02.861 --> 47:04.029
What are you gonna do then?

47:04.112 --> 47:06.073
I'll show her my translating device.

47:06.156 --> 47:08.450
- Good. You're doing well, Mr. Choi.
- [chuckles]

47:09.034 --> 47:11.245
Then what if you went to a coffee shop…

47:11.328 --> 47:13.914
[Yeon-su] Things are going
fairly smoothly, all things considered.

47:15.874 --> 47:18.460
Oh, Ye-in, can you please share
the presentation materials

47:18.544 --> 47:20.546
- with the rest of the team?
- Yes, ma'am, it's done.

47:20.629 --> 47:23.048
Hey, what's going on, you guys? Huh?

47:23.131 --> 47:25.592
How are you all so great at your jobs?
It's unbelievable.

47:25.676 --> 47:28.136
- I don't know what to do with you anymore.
- [all chuckling]

47:28.720 --> 47:30.931
I feel so ecstatic,
I can't hold myself back.

47:31.014 --> 47:33.183
- What do you say--
- [Yeon-su] No get-together today.

47:33.267 --> 47:34.726
I didn't even say anything.

47:34.810 --> 47:36.728
In case you forgot,
we just had one yesterday.

47:36.812 --> 47:38.730
If you keep this up,
I'll have to ban get-togethers again.

47:38.814 --> 47:41.191
"I'll ban get-togethers again." Geez.
[chuckles]

47:41.275 --> 47:43.360
Then how about
tomorrow evening? How's that?

47:43.443 --> 47:44.611
Tomorrow is Saturday.

47:44.695 --> 47:46.655
Okay. This coming Monday then,
after work, sounds good, right?

47:46.738 --> 47:49.408
We have a meeting.
All of us are… Well, not you, though.

47:49.491 --> 47:50.867
Oh.
[chuckles]

47:51.577 --> 47:52.452
Without me right?

47:53.412 --> 47:55.289
[I-hun] You already organized a meeting.

47:55.372 --> 47:57.165
Was everyone informed
that I wouldn't be attending?

47:57.749 --> 48:00.502
[Yeon-su] We focused on our lives
and did our best with what we had.

48:00.586 --> 48:03.380
And before we knew it,
time flew by in the blink of an eye.

48:03.463 --> 48:04.298
[sighs]

48:04.381 --> 48:07.426
You're being too careless.
Why'd you have to drink so much?

48:07.509 --> 48:08.969
You're not exactly at home, you know.

48:09.052 --> 48:11.179
Do you have any idea
how dangerous it could have been? Huh?

48:11.263 --> 48:12.598
- [Yeon-su] Of course…
- What would do if…

48:12.681 --> 48:14.933
…there were times
when we argued over and over.

48:15.517 --> 48:16.518
[scoffs]

48:16.602 --> 48:19.104
So you're not
gonna call me all day, are you Ung?

48:20.480 --> 48:23.108
Then I might just not pick up,
even if you try calling me.

48:25.652 --> 48:27.237
[phone buzzing]

48:29.448 --> 48:31.491
Yeah, hello? Ung?

48:31.575 --> 48:33.702
[Ung] Hmm. Been waiting a while?

48:34.453 --> 48:36.121
No, I wasn't waiting.

48:36.204 --> 48:38.665
Of course not. I wouldn't. As if. No way.

48:38.749 --> 48:41.627
[Ung chuckling]
Sorry. Been moving a lot the entire day.

48:42.294 --> 48:46.590
Hey you, communication is the core
of a long-distance relationship.

48:46.673 --> 48:48.925
If this keeps happening,
I'll be really hurt.

48:49.009 --> 48:50.719
It's gonna cause a misunderstanding.

48:50.802 --> 48:53.055
[Ung] I understand. Are you going home?

48:53.138 --> 48:56.016
Hmm. And you? Going home?

48:56.099 --> 48:58.352
To sleep?
Have you been sleeping well lately?

48:58.435 --> 49:00.395
And also, how's your eating schedule?

49:00.479 --> 49:02.648
[Ung] Don't you ever
get tired of asking me that?

49:02.731 --> 49:05.692
Do you? Why? Are you getting tired of me?

49:05.776 --> 49:07.944
[Ung] No, that's not what I meant.
Calm down.

49:08.028 --> 49:12.324
Geez, Yeon-su. You know,
you've been sulking a lot lately.

49:12.407 --> 49:14.993
Yeah. I've become pettier than ever.

49:16.119 --> 49:18.497
[sighs]
If only I'd known it'd be like this

49:18.580 --> 49:21.166
I would've hidden
your passport when you flew in last time.

49:21.667 --> 49:24.878
[Ung chuckles]
You've become a lot cuter too.

49:25.629 --> 49:28.799
[sighs]
I miss you so much, Ung.

49:31.593 --> 49:34.721
What? Why aren't you saying anything?

49:34.805 --> 49:35.972
[Ung] Yeon-su.

49:36.640 --> 49:40.560
Now that I think about it,
there was something I forgot to tell you.

49:40.644 --> 49:41.728
What is it?

49:45.440 --> 49:47.526
[audio falls away]

49:53.281 --> 49:54.533
What did you say?

49:55.325 --> 49:56.451
[Ung] You heard me.

49:58.620 --> 49:59.746
No, I didn't.

49:59.830 --> 50:02.249
I couldn't hear you properly,
so you have to say it again.

50:04.000 --> 50:05.210
[Ung] I love you.

50:09.756 --> 50:10.799
Do you…

50:14.052 --> 50:17.681
Do you even realize how long
it took for you to finally say that?

50:18.932 --> 50:22.894
Why didn't you… How come I've never
heard you say that to me before?

50:24.563 --> 50:27.232
[Ung] I love you, Yeon-su.

50:30.318 --> 50:32.654
You're such an idiot.
You know that, right?

50:34.239 --> 50:37.409
You supposed to say that in front of me.
You're unbelievable.

50:38.034 --> 50:39.119
[Ung] All right. Fine.

50:39.619 --> 50:40.996
Turn around and I will.

50:52.007 --> 50:55.302
["The Giving Tree"
by Lee Seung Yoon playing]

51:39.346 --> 51:40.514
You…

51:41.640 --> 51:42.557
Kook Yeon-su.

51:46.186 --> 51:47.395
I love you.

52:00.826 --> 52:02.285
What are you doing here?

52:02.911 --> 52:05.455
I missed you so much,
so I couldn't help it, I had to see you.

52:06.623 --> 52:08.375
But this is way too sudden.

52:09.000 --> 52:11.253
I didn't have a choice,
I had to tell you right now.

52:17.425 --> 52:18.593
[sighs in relief]

52:18.677 --> 52:22.472
Hey, I know the feeling, I can't handle
long-distance relationships.

52:22.556 --> 52:25.559
I know that.
That's why you should finish your studies.

52:25.642 --> 52:27.936
[Yeon-su] Otherwise,
can't you skip a year and come back?

52:28.019 --> 52:29.396
- I don't know.
- [Yeon-su sniffles]

52:29.479 --> 52:31.273
That's why I've been telling you.

52:31.356 --> 52:33.400
You should study hard
and try to graduate early.

52:33.483 --> 52:35.485
You can't keep
coming back and forth just to visit.

52:35.569 --> 52:37.487
It'll take ages for you
to just finish your studies.

52:37.571 --> 52:40.198
Hey, Yeon-su, are you
seriously nagging me right now?

52:40.282 --> 52:42.868
I'm not nagging,
I'm only saying this for our sake.

52:44.119 --> 52:46.496
["The Giving Tree" continuing]

52:57.173 --> 52:58.675
[Yeon-su] And there were also times…

53:02.804 --> 53:06.349
that I'd classify as
unbelievably phenomenal.

53:06.433 --> 53:07.601
That's how we were.

53:10.270 --> 53:13.148
["The Giving Tree" continuing]

53:31.541 --> 53:35.587
And that's the reason we were able
to stay strong all those years.

53:39.758 --> 53:42.218
And just like he promised from the start,

53:42.302 --> 53:46.139
he did it. And it didn't
take him too long, like he said.

53:52.896 --> 53:57.859
2 YEARS LATER

54:05.200 --> 54:06.242
[Eun-ho] Sol-i.

54:06.743 --> 54:07.661
Sol-i!

54:09.996 --> 54:11.873
- Hey, you.
- [Sol-i] Say what?

54:12.540 --> 54:16.002
- Don't "Hey you" me, you rude prick.
- We need to hurry up. We're already late.

54:16.086 --> 54:17.295
Did Ung's parents leave already?

54:17.379 --> 54:20.173
Yeah, they left ages ago.
We need to double time.

54:20.256 --> 54:21.341
Step aside.

54:21.424 --> 54:22.342
[Eun-ho groans]

54:23.051 --> 54:25.011
[cheeky music]

54:25.845 --> 54:28.682
- Have you been working out?
- What? That was nothing.

54:28.765 --> 54:30.684
They're pretty light.
Wrap it up and come out.

54:30.767 --> 54:32.310
- I'll go start the car.
- [Sol-i] Okay.

54:36.773 --> 54:37.899
[sighs in disbelief]

54:37.983 --> 54:40.694
I can't believe that kid has me
wrapped around his damn finger.

54:42.070 --> 54:43.863
He definitely has a crush on me,

54:43.947 --> 54:45.782
why won't he make his move?
It's been ages. Why?

54:45.865 --> 54:47.158
[Eun-ho] Come out already.

54:47.242 --> 54:48.201
Sheesh.

54:48.994 --> 54:50.412
You're like a pesky little child.

54:51.413 --> 54:54.040
Mr. Choi's parents
are such generous people, aren't they?

54:54.124 --> 54:57.210
They must've spent a hefty sum already
if they've been donating regularly.

54:57.877 --> 55:01.089
You're right.
I didn't know about it either,

55:01.172 --> 55:03.174
now I have more respect for those two.

55:04.259 --> 55:06.052
And Ms. Kook, is she going to be there?

55:06.136 --> 55:07.595
[chuckles softly]
I'm sure.

55:08.388 --> 55:12.434
Will you be okay? After all,
she is the girl that broke your heart.

55:12.517 --> 55:15.520
[chuckles]
Yep, and you never fail to remind me.

55:15.603 --> 55:18.106
Thanks, I almost forgot.
Can't wait for the next reminder.

55:20.025 --> 55:22.193
People are saying
you're starting to become like me,

55:22.277 --> 55:23.737
but maybe don't overdo it. Okay?

55:26.322 --> 55:28.324
- I need to say something.
- What now?

55:29.325 --> 55:30.535
And I'm only gonna say this

55:30.618 --> 55:32.620
because you seem
to be doing a lot better now.

55:34.956 --> 55:36.207
Just so you know, I like you.

55:37.709 --> 55:41.296
I'm only saying this because people
are saying I'm becoming more like you.

55:42.088 --> 55:43.882
And since you
never confessed your love to her,

55:45.633 --> 55:47.093
I'm not gonna be like you.

55:47.844 --> 55:48.887
[surprised exhale]

55:51.431 --> 55:53.516
That's all. Just saying, you know.

55:54.601 --> 55:56.436
[soft uplifting music]

55:57.896 --> 55:58.938
[chuckles softly]

56:05.236 --> 56:06.946
MUSIC LIBRARY

56:08.740 --> 56:09.866
BOOK DONATION WITH UNG

56:10.492 --> 56:11.701
TWOO TWIT
THE RED DOG OF THE DARK

56:11.785 --> 56:14.871
WITH UNG

56:16.372 --> 56:17.707
[classical piece playing]

56:18.208 --> 56:21.419
- [Yeon-ok] Over here. Come on, guys!
- Come on, let's go.

56:23.588 --> 56:26.800
Sol-i, I'm hungry.
What are we eating, huh?

56:26.883 --> 56:28.218
What the heck are you asking me that for?

56:28.301 --> 56:29.719
Don't you wanna go on a date?

56:29.803 --> 56:31.763
BOOK DONATION WITH UNG

56:32.472 --> 56:33.473
Okay then, I'm ready.

56:36.267 --> 56:38.103
[Sol-i] So that's why
he's been working out.

56:41.064 --> 56:43.775
[Ho] Okay. It's very nice to meet you.

56:43.858 --> 56:46.986
I'm sorry I'm a little embarrassed,
because this isn't really my thing.

56:47.070 --> 56:50.365
I believe everyone should be doing this
and as a member of society,

56:50.448 --> 56:53.618
I'm just doing my part.
It's a small contribution to help out.

56:53.701 --> 56:56.579
[Ho] Oh, my goodness, I'm so embarrassed.

56:56.663 --> 56:59.999
Uh… My son loved books.
Which is why we had so many.

57:00.083 --> 57:01.626
As a boy, he'd always be reading.

57:01.709 --> 57:03.878
And we would go on for hours.
He takes after me.

57:03.962 --> 57:06.256
- I hope all kids would have the chance--
- Hey, Ung.

57:06.339 --> 57:07.590
[Ho] Come on, not again!

57:07.674 --> 57:10.009
[Yeon-ok] You're so late.
I told you to come early and help out.

57:10.093 --> 57:12.595
I've been carrying these
since this morning, trust me.

57:12.679 --> 57:14.055
- Is that true?
- [Ung] Yes.

57:14.139 --> 57:15.473
It always turns into a blooper

57:15.557 --> 57:17.684
and we need to do a retake
whenever Ung pops in.

57:17.767 --> 57:19.769
Hey, you get some sleep?

57:19.853 --> 57:21.187
How long do you usually marinate pork?

57:21.271 --> 57:22.522
I don't know. For eight hours?

57:22.605 --> 57:25.442
Well, I slept for ten hours.
Even longer than marinated pork.

57:25.525 --> 57:27.444
- Oh, what a good boy!
- [Yeon-su] Hello everyone!

57:27.527 --> 57:28.987
- [Ho] Hey, Yeon-su.
- Yeon-su.

57:29.487 --> 57:30.655
I told you not to go, what are you doing?

57:30.738 --> 57:32.407
You should be resting on weekends.

57:32.490 --> 57:34.826
I'm okay. I should help out anyway.
So where do I put this down?

57:34.909 --> 57:36.119
Upstairs.

57:36.202 --> 57:38.705
[Ho] Yeon-su, just put yours
on top of Ung's. He'll handle it.

57:38.788 --> 57:39.706
Hurry, help her.

57:41.040 --> 57:41.875
[chuckles]

57:41.958 --> 57:45.336
BOOK DONATION WITH UNG

57:46.129 --> 57:48.006
[cheerful bubbly music]

57:51.176 --> 57:53.052
[yawns loudly]

57:56.222 --> 57:58.224
Don't you think
you're just oversleeping nowadays?

57:58.308 --> 58:01.060
Once the exhibition begins,
I won't be getting enough.

58:01.144 --> 58:02.937
So I should sleep while I still can.

58:03.646 --> 58:05.940
[Ung groans]
How long is this gonna take?

58:06.024 --> 58:09.402
Don't be lazy. Stop putting them wherever.
Make sure to put them in the right order.

58:09.486 --> 58:10.653
I'll be watching you.

58:12.530 --> 58:14.157
[cheerful bubbly music]

58:25.251 --> 58:29.464
Somehow this all feels too familiar.
Reminds you of high school, doesn't it?

58:29.547 --> 58:31.841
Isn't that memory
a little too old to remember?

58:32.842 --> 58:36.513
Not really. Still vivid in my head.
As if it only happened yesterday.

58:38.181 --> 58:40.141
Frankly, same here.

58:42.435 --> 58:43.561
[chuckles softly]

58:45.563 --> 58:46.731
Tell me the truth for once.

58:47.357 --> 58:48.191
About?

58:48.775 --> 58:51.945
About you having a crush on me
when we first met.

58:52.028 --> 58:53.655
[scoffs, breathes in sharply]

58:53.738 --> 58:56.824
There you go, manipulating
your memory for your benefit again.

58:56.908 --> 58:58.117
Nah-uh!

58:58.201 --> 59:00.912
Don't deny it, I could see it
in your eyes. It was obvious.

59:00.995 --> 59:03.540
[scoffs]
Yeah, don't make me laugh.

59:03.623 --> 59:06.376
You sure you're not the one
who fell in love with me at first sight?

59:06.459 --> 59:08.670
That's why you followed me around, right?

59:09.254 --> 59:11.297
When was it that I saw you
for the first time?

59:11.881 --> 59:13.216
Was it the first day of filming?

59:13.883 --> 59:15.635
- Hey.
- Or was it before that?

59:17.011 --> 59:19.973
I know you're just pretending
like you don't remember when it was.

59:36.906 --> 59:39.367
Hey, we're supposed
to be putting books in.

59:39.450 --> 59:40.952
What have you been doing?

59:41.035 --> 59:42.787
Why would you doodle on that?

59:42.870 --> 59:44.122
You're not a kid.

59:44.205 --> 59:45.540
I LOVE EARLY SUMMER
LEE NA-EUN

59:46.165 --> 59:47.625
What did you draw in this?

59:56.342 --> 59:57.677
[Ung] Unforgettable.

59:58.678 --> 01:00:01.264
Everyone has one
from a certain time in their life.

01:00:01.931 --> 01:00:03.349
["Christmas Tree" by V playing]

01:00:06.144 --> 01:00:09.689
Those memories you cherish so much
every waking moment

01:00:09.772 --> 01:00:11.357
will last you for a lifetime.

01:00:16.279 --> 01:00:17.280
Kook Yeon-su.

01:00:20.408 --> 01:00:22.410
Our year hasn't even ended yet…

01:00:24.954 --> 01:00:30.460
♪ Your light's the only thing
That keeps the cold out ♪

01:00:31.127 --> 01:00:34.547
♪ Moon in the summer night ♪

01:00:34.631 --> 01:00:37.592
♪ Whispering of the stars ♪

01:00:38.301 --> 01:00:39.927
…and our life has barely begun.

01:00:43.306 --> 01:00:45.725
[Ung] Marry me, Yeon-su.

01:00:47.352 --> 01:00:53.399
EPILOGUE

01:01:00.782 --> 01:01:01.991
Ready to film?

01:01:04.535 --> 01:01:06.746
What? What did you just say?

01:01:07.246 --> 01:01:08.706
You're gonna have to, it's all your fault.

01:01:08.790 --> 01:01:10.500
What are you nuts? It's not happening.

01:01:11.793 --> 01:01:14.253
Your last documentary
is back from the dead and popular.

01:01:14.337 --> 01:01:15.963
Why the hell'd you have to get married?

01:01:16.047 --> 01:01:17.924
Too bad, now they all
wanna watch your married life.

01:01:18.007 --> 01:01:20.760
Are you crazy? Aren't we ever
gonna have some sort of privacy?

01:01:21.260 --> 01:01:23.721
Hey, what do you take us for,
a couple of pushovers you can boss around?

01:01:24.722 --> 01:01:25.890
- Hello everyone.
- Hello everyone.

01:01:25.973 --> 01:01:27.308
I'm Choi Ung.

01:01:28.476 --> 01:01:29.477
I'm Kook Yeon-su.

01:01:31.312 --> 01:01:32.647
[chuckle softly]

01:01:33.231 --> 01:01:34.399
One, two, three.

01:01:34.482 --> 01:01:36.234
[both] So, we're married now.

01:01:36.859 --> 01:01:38.111
[chuckles]

01:01:49.872 --> 01:01:53.042
["Christmas Tree" by V playing]
